{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Independent review of PR #411 found concurrent ACP connection setup could launch multiple agent processes, and stderr redaction could emit a secret fragment split across pipe-read boundaries. The review also requested explicit launcher diagnostics, shutdown cancellation, and a guard against overwriting same-Timeline active Turn state.","decision":"Memoize and share one connection-establishment Task per backend, cancel and await it during shutdown after marking active Turns cancelled, prevent a Turn from becoming active after shutdown or replacing an existing same-Timeline Turn, and retain the longest stderr suffix that could be a secret prefix before emitting output. Name and validate the Perl process-group launcher and mention it in startup diagnostics.","impact":"Concurrent startup now owns one child and shutdown joins in-flight setup before closing resources. Stderr redaction handles matches spanning reads. Backend/RuntimeEffectScope boundaries and bounded retirement remain unchanged. The code continues to use bounded graceful/forced waits followed by waitUntilExit to reap the child.","recurrence_control":"New regressions cover concurrent first connection, shutdown during initialization, straddling redaction, and same-Timeline concurrent Turns. make acp-smoke, make verify, make runner-smoke, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":["Independently start a child for every caller with no shared establishment flight, which can orphan a process when stored references are overwritten."],"sources":[]}
